posting. One of them advised against using a non-DEC drive for a system
disk in strong language. The other one replied that it should work fine,
as long as the particular SCSI drive implements all of the MODE SELECT
SCSI parameters and is smaller than 1.07GB (pre VMS 5.4), and cautioned me
about keeping my cluster system disk reliable. VMS began supporting 3rd 
party SCSI devices under VMS 5.3.

