>running PSI.
Well, running PSI is OK, since that is pure X.25. Our X.25 switching support would let you connect the VAXen, and use PSI mail for mail, and the SET HOST/X29 command for virtual terminal access. You could even use DECnet between your VAXen that have PSI support. What you *can't* do is DECnet routing compatibly with PSI over X.25. However, you could configure some VAX as a router to make this work.

