and feels just like SunView.  That's what I meant.

Frankly, I'm really unhappy with Sun's marketing things.  They've pulled
the ol' "buzzword idiot trap."  Now, you'll ask, what is a "buzzword
idiot trap."

Well, it's like this.  OSF Motif is the industry standard.  Period.
It's from the "Open Systems Foundation."  You'll notice the word "open"
beginning to pop up here as often as the word "the".  It's the hot
buzzword.

Since Sun decided to not go with the industry standard (and they knew Motif
would be the standard), they had to make up for it in some other way.
There'd be too many people looking for "open systems", even though they
didn't know what it meant.  So, the marketing things invented another
"buzzword idiot trap."  They put the word "open" into the name of their
windowing interface.  Idiots buy them because they see their buzzword
there.  "OpenLook!  Wow, must be one of them open systems!  That's what
we want, 'cause open systems are better!"

I'm not dumping on Sun.  Their hardward and software are both fine.
But, I don't see using a "BIT" as a fair marketing strategy.  The bottom
line is this:  It's meant to confuse people who don't know better.  Too
bad they resorted to such tactics...

