Do you have TCP/IP on your VAX? If so, whose? TGV's Multinet includes an RMT
server that will work with remote tar on a unix host, and will allow you to do
what you want. DECnet includes no such capability, so if you are connecting to
the VAX via DECnet from the sun, you are stuck. People _have_ implemented this
sort of capability for DECnet, and I'm sure it is on a DECUS tape somewhere, but
you'd have to build a unix client end for it. I've never heard of this sort of
thing over DECnet from unix to VMS, but that, of course, doesn't prove
anything.

