Somebody suggested that a 386 box is a better hobbyist machine than
a PDP11. Well, as the owner of a PDP11/45 and 2 * PDP11/10's, I much
prefer them to anything with an intel processor. Why ? 
The PDP11's are 
a) Well designed. The UNIBUS is much better than ISA - look at the 
interupts or DMA for a start.
b) Documented. I have schematics for my CPU, and peripherals.
Also, Microcode source. Try getting that for a 386 machine!
c) the disk drives are demountable. If I have head trouble, I strip the
drive and
replace the head. I don't have to replace the whole drive.
The instruction set is also much better than anything Intel has designed
IMHO. I wouldn't swap for anything !!!!!!


But, I wish that DEC would licence me an OS for a reasonable ammount. 
Toggling in code on the front panel gets painful after a while,
although I prefer the panel to most debuggers. Anybody got any
suggestions as to where I can get an OS, or a licence cheap ?? :-)

