My experience with PDP-11/34s tells me that you've got one of three problems:

1.  You don't have a bus grant card in each unused slot (or you've got one in
backwards.  If you're pretty new to Unibus PDP-11s, the bus grant cards are
those little 3"x3" jobs, and you've got to have one in the "D" region of each
unused slot.

2.  You've got a DMA card (DMA is called NPR by DEC) that doesn't have it's
NPG jumper removed.  The jumper is between pins CA1 and CB1 on the backplane.
If you've never worked on this problem before, you ought to get assistance the
first time you try it.  DMA cards include disk controllers, Ethernet controllers
and so on.

3.  You've got a non-DMA card in a slot that has the DMA jumper removed.  This
is the same jumper mentioned in 2.  Non-DMA cards are cards like your DL-11
that runs the console terminal, LP-11 printer controllers, etc.

