Hmmm. My PDPs *hang* on bad NPR/NPG signals...

To check for BUS GRANT signals reduce your machine step-by-step: move
the terminator as near to the CPU as possible (put is where the M930
leaves the CPU backplane). Continue step-by-step rebuilding towards the
end.

M930's can be tired as well... Are the small grant cards properly located?
XXDP can run on fairly sick machines (that's what doctor's have to): it
tries to avoid DMA where possible.

Anyway: stopping the 1134a from console will not likely generate DMA
activity.

