I have the same kind of probems. It occurs every time when
an application which uses the xview library running on a sun
is displayed through the DEC X-server.

The problems can be divided in two:

1. The sun fonts:
	The DEC server can't find the requested font
	(they are on the sun) 
   Solution (short description): 
	Copy the sun fonts (-sun-*-*.... and -b&h-*-*.....)
	to the DEC.
	-take the BDF format from the tape
	-copy
	-convert to DEC's PCF
	-rehash your fontpath. 
	The names of the commands differ slightly from sun to
	DEC, "apropos font | grep \(1\)" gets then names.

2. The Atom problem.
	The "Atom problem" occurs in slightly different shapes 
	in connection with twm and dxwm. With twm the application
	dies when the cursor is moved into the window, with dxwm
	it dies when the window is moved.
	Typical error printout:

		octopus>calctool
		X Error:  BadAtom
		  Request Major code 17 ()
		  Request Minor code 0
		  ResourceID 0x782310		#Allways BIG number#
		  Error Serial #683
		  Current Serial #683
		octopus>
	
	The strange thing is that "normal" behavior doesn't produce
	any atom request at all.
    Solution:
	None yet.
    Guess: 
	The bite order gets mixed up somewhere - but I don't know 
	where when or why.

Suggestions of any kind are welcome. There will be 170 students trying 
to use xview programs displayed on DEC 2100 in november.

Thanks for listening to my problems,
Harald
