are used.  News software is installed on Sun workstations, but not on
VMS.  Our UNIX boxes and VAXen can communicate using either TCP/IP
(Suns or DECstation) or DECnet (DECstations only); but the VAXen don't
use all TCP protocols (e.g. no SMTP mail); however DECnet mail between
the VAXen and UNIX boxes works fine.  Both VAXen also run the NFS
server portion of UCX, allowing VAX disks to be mounted on UNIX
workstations.  In short, files can be moved between the machines in a
variety of ways.

For better or worse, VAXNOTES is the official company conferencing
system.  But since I have two UNIX workstations on my desk, I would
rather not have to log into a VAX to use VAXNOTES.  What I would like
is to use news on a UNIX machine to fully access everything in the
VAXNOTES system on the VMS boxes.  This means that ideally, all of the
following would be possible
   * articles posted to VAXNOTES can be read as news
   * articles posted to news can be read in VAXNOTES
   * mail replies to VAXNOTES articles in news work properly
   * mail replies to news articles in VAXNOTES work properly 
My primary interest is accessing VAXNOTES conferences from news, not
accessing general USENET articles from VAXNOTES.

