I did just what you described but found that the EWS software that was
developed doesn't really turn a 2000 into a VT1300.  The 2000 still requires
a VAX/VMS system to be the boot host and more importantly the X-windows
host for that 2000.  I couldn't get the system to create LAT sessions (which
a VT1300 does) but all Xterm session were on the VAX host.  Once I SET HOST
to other systems, I could use SET DISPLAY/NODE= to send an Xterm display
to the 2000.  Since I wanted the system for a multi-windowing terminal
rather than a Xterminal, it was more useful as a satellite in a MIcluster.
The performance hit for the windows was on the 2000 rather than on the
serving VAX.

I don't know if there's a Ultrix version of the EWS software and if you'll
need DECnet installed (definitely required for VMS, don't know for Ultrix).

If you don't have a VMS system to be host for EWS, don't waste your time.
