In article <28467244@zl2tnm.gp.co.nz>, don@zl2tnm.gp.co.nz (Don Stokes) writes:
> Two VAXstation questions:
> 
> (1) What are the identifying marks on a VCB01 vs VCB02?  

  The VCB01 has a distribution panel with two DB-15's (one male, one female).
The VCB02 has a single DB-15. The VCB01 is always a single board, with a rib-
bon cable and a coax connecting the distribution panel to the board. The VCB02
is either 2 or 3 boards, with a fat ribbon cable and a skinny one running be-
tween the boards. It connects to the distribution panel with coaxial cables,
no ribbon cable.

> (2) Given a VAXstation II with with one of the above boards, a TQK50, 
> RQDX3, and DEQNA (I know, I know!), what (and how) should one set up the
> vector & CSR for a DHV11 (8 line terminal mux)?  I don't have hardware 
> docs; all this gear is (very) secondhand, home system etc.... (service 
> contracts?)  The device can be seen (TXA0-TXA7), but times out if you 
> try to use it -- I'd put it down to correct CSR but incorrect vector.
> The board came out of an 11/73 with naff all additional hardware (cpu,
> memory & RQDX3); its vector was 310.

  It depends. VMS keeps changing the rules. The best bet is to ask SYSGEN
CONFIGURE what it wants.

