In article <1465@nddsun1.sps.mot.com> I write:
>
>  Beware of using the Fuji with Ultrix 4.2 as the system boot drive!
>Prior to Ultrix 4.2, the Fuji worked fine as a second rz56 on my
>DS5000/200; I was using a "b" partition on the Fuji as a second swap
>space.  Now 4.2 won't recognize the Fuji drive swap partition, even
>though I have no trouble with it as a data drive.  Messages from the
>...

Thanks to Robert Chesler, rtc@westford.ccur.com, who solved the problem.

Bricks to DEC support, who were not any help whatsoever.

The solution is to add the following code fragment to "/sys/data/scsi_data.c",
then rebuild the kernel and reboot:

/* [ FUJITSU _M2263S-512       0168 ] Fuji SCSI 660 */
{"FUJITSU M2263S-512", 18, DEV_RZ56, RZ56, sz_rz56_sizes, 0, 0,
	 SCSI_TRYSYNC | SCSI_STARTUNIT
#ifdef mips
	 | SCSI_REQSNS | SCSI_TESTUNITREADY | SCSI_READCAPACITY
#endif mips
	 , 0 },
/* ---------------- */

This code allows the Fuji drive to get recognized as a true RZ56 with
all its capabilities etc.

I wonder if DEC will ever have more than about two people working on
Ultrix?  Seems like whenever they get someone starting to know a little
non-VMS, he up and quits. I wonder why?

